  "targets": {
    "howTitle": "How the planner uses these",
    "howBody": "<b>Hard min / hard max</b> are inviolable bounds — the planner will not propose a dose program whose predicted irrigation ppm crosses them. <b>Soft target</b> is the goal. <b>Priority</b> (1=highest, 5=lowest) weighs how aggressively the planner minimizes deviation from the soft target. When ingredients are coupled (e.g. Ca-nitrate delivers both Ca and N), higher-priority elements override lower-priority ones — at duty=100% Ca might hit 150 ppm while N reaches 139 ppm even if N's soft target is 100 ppm, as long as N stays under its hard max.",
    "groups": {
      "elemental": {
        "label": "Elemental (computed from tank composition)",
        "description": "% by weight, derived from each ingredient's elemental composition. Used by the planner when computing predicted irrigation ppm from dose programs."
